# guard-page control 2 (R65): the property proof "bigint divmod reconstruct"
# before R65 allocated 8 cells and then compared 16. A READ past the block, no
# write at all. Under GUARD_PAGES the read of cell 8 must fault.
# R77: since v274 the language itself refuses this read when the size is a written number
# (`nirmmita(8 * 8)`: mala ank seema atikram, exit 1), before the guard page is reached. The size is
# computed here so that this stays a control of the GUARD PAGE, which is what it is for.
mukhya() {
    vitti cells = 8
    vitti a = nirmmita(cells * 8)
    vitti s = 0
    vitti i = 0
    yavat (i < 16) {
        s = s + a[i]
        i = i + 1
    }
    likha(s)
}
